cpmemu for Debian: notes on the source
=======================================

Prebuilt test programs
----------------------

tests/ holds CP/M test programs (.com, and .bin images of the same code)
next to their source.  The Debian build does not assemble them again,
because the tools that built them are not in Debian:

 * The .com and .bin files beside tests/*.asm were assembled upstream with
   z88dk's z80asm ("z88dk.z88dk-z80asm -b", docs/test_suite.md).  Some
   headers name another assembler: test_ixh.asm names z80asm,
   test_alu_minimal.asm names asm8080, and test_djnz.asm names um80 and
   ul80.  tests/flag_test.com and tests/flag_test.hex are assembled by hand
   by tests/make_test.sh.

 * tests/8080/*.com are copied from https://github.com/superzazu/8080
   (cpu_tests).  The .prn files beside them are their Microsoft MACRO-80
   3.44 listings, and the .mac files are the source.

 * tests/zexdoc.com and tests/zexall.com are copied byte-identical from
   https://github.com/agn453/ZEXALL.  tests/zexdoc.mac and tests/zexall.mac
   are the source; their headers say to assemble them with Hector Peraza's
   ZSM4.

Other .asm files in tests/ have no committed binary: tests/run_tests.sh
assembles them at test time with um80 and ul80, the upstream project's own
assembler and linker (https://github.com/avwohl/um80_and_friends, not in
Debian).  When um80 is not installed, those groups of checks skip and the
suite still exits 0.  So does the group of tests/cpm-test, a git submodule
that is empty in the release tarball.

The build runs tests/run_tests.sh, which runs the prebuilt programs under
the emulator it just built, and util/test_cpm_disk.py.

 -- Aaron Wohl <xdeb@awohl.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:10:00 -0500
